1
00:00:06,964 --> 00:00:09,009
[Dustin] And then I got in the car
to come here,

2
00:00:09,092 --> 00:00:12,345
and I'm putting on my seat belt,
and I hear my shoulder pop.

3
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:15,182
I mean, I hear my body making
bad noises all day.

4
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:18,101
-[Dr. Powell] Well, you're getting older.
-Yeah. I'm getting older.

5
00:00:18,185 --> 00:00:20,978
[sighs] It's got me thinking that, um...

6
00:00:21,896 --> 00:00:25,150
I don't know, when I'm on my death bed
and someone is deciding to pull the plug,

7
00:00:25,233 --> 00:00:29,529
I want it to be my kid,
not my pool guy, you know?

8
00:00:29,612 --> 00:00:30,697
Not that I have a pool, but...

9
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:31,989
"My kid."

10
00:00:32,074 --> 00:00:33,908
Did you notice
that you just said "my kid"?

11
00:00:33,991 --> 00:00:36,536
[chuckles] Well, yeah, I mean, I...

12
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:37,829
[inhales sharply]

13
00:00:37,912 --> 00:00:40,748
I've been thinking lately
that maybe I want to start a family.

14
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:44,711
What exactly is going on between you
and Mickey right now?

15
00:00:44,794 --> 00:00:45,962
-How is it?
-Great.

16
00:00:46,045 --> 00:00:47,130
I mean...

17
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:50,759
obviously things went bad
the first time around, but...

18
00:00:51,593 --> 00:00:53,886
I don't know. Feels different this time.

19
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:56,181
I like hearing this.
It's what I've been drilling here.

20
00:00:56,264 --> 00:00:57,765
You deserve to be happy.

21
00:00:57,849 --> 00:01:02,354
You... you need to feel entitled
to your own happiness.

22
00:01:03,062 --> 00:01:04,314
Yeah.

23
00:01:04,397 --> 00:01:06,274
No, definitely. I'm...

24
00:01:08,401 --> 00:01:11,071
I am entitled to be
in a relationship with Mickey.

25
00:01:11,154 --> 00:01:12,614
I mean, that's what I want.

26
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:15,492
I can't fuck this up again.

27
00:01:15,575 --> 00:01:17,619
Okay. Well, that's your time.

28
00:01:17,702 --> 00:01:20,455
-And I'm gonna see you next week, okay?
-Okay.

29
00:01:20,538 --> 00:01:21,748
Just a little FYI.

30
00:01:21,831 --> 00:01:25,502
I'm having this mindfulness retreat
at Esalen next month.

31
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:29,839
No pressure, but if you and Mickey felt
that it would be, uh,

32
00:01:29,922 --> 00:01:31,383
valuable to you two...

33
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:33,468
[stutters] I'll run it by her.

34
00:01:33,551 --> 00:01:35,678
Uh, the meals are included in the price.

35
00:01:36,263 --> 00:01:38,265
[theme music playing]

36
00:01:56,073 --> 00:01:57,534
We need to change the music
on this show.

37
00:01:57,617 --> 00:02:01,078
I mean, every time we do a serious moment,
they play violins.

38
00:02:01,163 --> 00:02:02,997
It makes me want to claw
my fucking ears off.

39
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:05,082
Okay, Mickey. Can I just do this?

40
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:08,920
Whoo! I just talked to Business Affairs

41
00:02:09,003 --> 00:02:10,630
and Stella's deal is closed.

42
00:02:10,713 --> 00:02:14,717
So, she is officially part
of the Gravity Subzero family. [chuckles]

43
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:16,469
Wow! That's...

44
00:02:17,845 --> 00:02:19,264
Wow, that's cool. [chuckles]

45
00:02:19,347 --> 00:02:20,682
You made our asses look good.

46
00:02:20,765 --> 00:02:21,891
That's 'cause I'm hot shit.

47
00:02:21,974 --> 00:02:24,686
Well, your hot shit came out of
our lame asses. [laughs]

48
00:02:24,811 --> 00:02:26,313
[Dr. Greg chuckles softly]

49
00:02:26,896 --> 00:02:29,023
I just wanted to give you the good news.

50
00:02:29,106 --> 00:02:31,984
And, so, later, just swing by my office,
okay? Yes!

51
00:02:33,110 --> 00:02:34,612
Well...

52
00:02:34,696 --> 00:02:36,489
congrats, Mickey. [chuckles]

53
00:02:36,573 --> 00:02:39,075
Thanks. I know you don't mean that,
but, whatever.

54
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:40,743
No, I do. Seriously.

55
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:42,537
Bravo.

56
00:02:44,038 --> 00:02:47,375
Thank you. I, uh, appreciate that. Um...

57
00:02:50,127 --> 00:02:51,629
That's... that's nice.

58
00:02:54,924 --> 00:02:56,218
It's funny, huh?

59
00:02:56,301 --> 00:02:59,929
Sometimes it's hard for us
to accept a compliment, right?

60
00:03:01,223 --> 00:03:02,807
I'm wired the same way, too.

61
00:03:02,890 --> 00:03:06,478
Yeah, I don't know. It's hard to accept
a pat on the back at work,

62
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:09,272
when you're shitting the bed
in the rest of your life.

63
00:03:09,356 --> 00:03:11,233
-Oh.
-[sighs]

64
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:13,943
What's wrong? Something up?

65
00:03:14,026 --> 00:03:16,863
-Oh, like I would ever tell you.
-Oh, come on.

66
00:03:16,946 --> 00:03:19,991
[stutters] Look, I know
that we used to clash, but...

67
00:03:21,033 --> 00:03:23,035
remember how we used to get along?

68
00:03:23,119 --> 00:03:27,164
You know, I'd really things to go back
to being like that.

69
00:03:27,249 --> 00:03:29,083
Supportive, kind.

70
00:03:29,166 --> 00:03:31,878
You know, really...
really there for each other.

71
00:03:33,588 --> 00:03:35,089
Okay, um...

72
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:40,386
Well, Gus went out of town for work,
and it was really hard.

73
00:03:41,679 --> 00:03:43,931
And then I started seeing an ex...

74
00:03:44,932 --> 00:03:47,227
and then he got super clingy,

75
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:51,939
and now, Gus is back in town
and I don't know what to do.

76
00:03:52,023 --> 00:03:54,817
Wow. That's a...
a lot to unpack there. Hmm?

77
00:03:54,901 --> 00:03:56,110
Yeah.

78
00:04:00,197 --> 00:04:02,325
So, what do you think?
Do you have any advice?

79
00:04:02,409 --> 00:04:04,244
Oh, I don't really have any advice.

80
00:04:04,327 --> 00:04:05,828
I don't know what I could give.

81
00:04:05,912 --> 00:04:07,289
You're a fucking nightmare. [chuckles]

82
00:04:07,372 --> 00:04:08,873
-Excuse me?
-I'm sorry, no.

83
00:04:08,956 --> 00:04:11,626
[stutters] I didn't mean it
to come out that way.

84
00:04:13,127 --> 00:04:15,547
-Uh, just, please go.
-Yeah.

85
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:18,215
But, hey. Maybe it's a good thing
that we said it out loud.

86
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:19,426
You said it.

87
00:04:20,051 --> 00:04:22,720
Yeah. But... now it's out there.

88
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:25,390
So, you can address it. [chuckles softly]

89
00:04:27,099 --> 00:04:29,644
Excuse me, I'm gonna go get a donut.
[chuckles nervously]

90
00:04:29,727 --> 00:04:33,189
But seriously, [stutters]
I still want you to talk to me if you...

91
00:04:33,272 --> 00:04:34,566
Right.

92
00:04:38,069 --> 00:04:39,612
[Chris] Hey, everybody listen up!

93
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:42,031
-Cruikshank's back, motherfucker!
-[all cheer]

94
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:44,659
Whoo!

95
00:04:44,742 --> 00:04:46,035
Hey!

96
00:04:46,118 --> 00:04:50,247
-All right, hey, guys. Oh. I'll do it.
-Gus, my boy!

97
00:04:51,165 --> 00:04:52,500
Put it down. Let's get a picture.

98
00:04:52,584 --> 00:04:55,462
-Chris! Come on, get a picture with us.
-[Chris] All right, all right.

99
00:04:55,545 --> 00:04:58,465
-A group pic on three. One, two, three...
-[camera clicks]

100
00:04:58,548 --> 00:04:59,799
[Gus] And four.

101
00:04:59,882 --> 00:05:03,720
[all singing]
♪ They say that the cider house sucks ♪

102
00:05:05,012 --> 00:05:07,515
♪ But they're all fools ♪

103
00:05:08,975 --> 00:05:13,229
♪ 'Cause what they don't know is
The cider house rocks ♪

104
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:18,610
♪ And the cider house rules ♪

105
00:05:20,152 --> 00:05:23,615
♪ And the cider house rules ♪

106
00:05:23,698 --> 00:05:25,032
One more time.

107
00:05:25,116 --> 00:05:30,037
♪ And the cider house rules ♪

108
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:36,586
How are you, dude?
How was working on, uh, Liberty Is Free?

109
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:38,045
-Oh, Liberty Down.
-Yeah.

110
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:40,465
Yeah. It was, uh... It was okay.

111
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:43,551
You know, it's just a little tough
being away from home.

112
00:05:43,635 --> 00:05:45,470
-Being away from Mickey.
-Ah...

113
00:05:45,553 --> 00:05:47,597
Bertie said Mickey was having
a hard time with it, too.

114
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,348
-Oh, she said that?
-Yeah.

115
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:52,351
Yeah, well, I don't know.
I mean, at first...

116
00:05:52,685 --> 00:05:54,687
[inhales sharply] At first, it was fine.

117
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:56,481
-We were talking every day.
-Uh-huh.

118
00:05:56,564 --> 00:05:58,065
-It was going well.
-Mmm-hmm.

119
00:05:58,149 --> 00:06:01,403
And then, by the end there,
we weren't, like, talking at all.

120
00:06:01,486 --> 00:06:03,195
-Oh, man...
-And I started...

121
00:06:03,279 --> 00:06:06,658
getting the vibe of, like,
"Oh, she's not into this anymore,

122
00:06:06,741 --> 00:06:09,702
and she wants it to be over."

123
00:06:09,786 --> 00:06:11,954
But then, last night she texted me,

124
00:06:12,038 --> 00:06:15,082
and wanted to see if I wanted
to hang out tomorrow, so...

125
00:06:15,166 --> 00:06:16,167
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Awesome.

126
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:19,003
I don't want to, like,
pat myself on the back here too hard.

127
00:06:19,086 --> 00:06:21,589
But those last few days in Atlanta,

128
00:06:21,673 --> 00:06:26,010
you know, I just... I took a step back,
and I gave her her space.

129
00:06:26,093 --> 00:06:30,181
And I think that's, like, why she's
texting me now, you know? It worked.

130
00:06:30,264 --> 00:06:32,559
Yeah, me and Bertie
were kind of like the same thing.

131
00:06:32,642 --> 00:06:36,062
Like, we broke up,
and I was home crying all the time.

132
00:06:36,145 --> 00:06:38,898
And then I didn't call her
'cause I was gonna kill myself.

133
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:40,650
She thought that I was giving her space.

134
00:06:40,733 --> 00:06:43,360
-Mmm-hmm.
-So, she got back with me.

135
00:06:43,445 --> 00:06:46,405
Oh, look at us, man.
We are, like, killing it.

136
00:06:46,489 --> 00:06:48,074
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

137
00:06:48,658 --> 00:06:51,035
All right, well,
I'm gonna get back to this party.

138
00:06:51,118 --> 00:06:53,705
You can stay here if you like.
[grunts] Nice and comfy.

139
00:06:53,788 --> 00:06:55,582
Yeah. The coats are comfy.

140
00:06:56,624 --> 00:06:57,750
Hey, Gus.

141
00:06:57,834 --> 00:07:02,088
If I borrowed, like, $100 from you,
I could pay you back $110 later on.

142
00:07:02,171 --> 00:07:06,342
-If you were cool with that.
-Oh. Yeah, maybe.

143
00:07:06,425 --> 00:07:10,054
Or, you know what, I'm trying to sell
my Nintendo 64, if you're interested.

144
00:07:10,137 --> 00:07:12,223
-Let's talk about it later.
-Okay.

145
00:07:12,306 --> 00:07:14,809
-Get back to this party. Okay.
-Cool.

146
00:07:18,312 --> 00:07:19,313
[sighs]

147
00:07:19,396 --> 00:07:20,815
[Frank] Adiós, amigo.

148
00:07:20,898 --> 00:07:23,025
-Bye-bye. See you.
-You gotta drop by our place again.

149
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:25,027
We got some new speakers,
and I'm serious,

150
00:07:25,111 --> 00:07:26,988
you put on Houses of the Holy, right,

151
00:07:27,071 --> 00:07:29,866
and it sounds like Zep's playing
in your living room.

152
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:30,950
Wow.

153
00:07:31,033 --> 00:07:33,745
-Well, sign me up. I... I'll be by soon.
-[Frank] We gotta go.

154
00:07:33,828 --> 00:07:35,455
Getting out of here, too, man.

155
00:07:35,538 --> 00:07:38,457
Okay, Kev, and uh, hey, now that
I'm back in town, we gotta hang out.

156
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:40,001
-For sure.
-Yeah, I'm gonna turn this

157
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:42,086
work friendship into a real friendship.

158
00:07:42,169 --> 00:07:43,963
There's nothing you can do about it.
Sorry.

159
00:07:44,046 --> 00:07:45,757
It's all good.
I already knew we were friends.

160
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:47,383
Ever since you started coming
to the snack table

161
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:49,677
-when you didn't want somethin'.
-Yeah, that's a telltale sign.

162
00:07:49,761 --> 00:07:50,928
-I knew what was up.
-Yeah, you knew.

163
00:07:51,012 --> 00:07:52,555
-All right. Bye, buddy.
-See you soon, man.

164
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:53,973
Oh, Gus. I forgot to tell you.

165
00:07:54,056 --> 00:07:56,476
We saw your little sweetheart
the other day.

166
00:07:56,559 --> 00:07:57,769
-That's right.
-[Gus] You did?

167
00:07:57,852 --> 00:08:00,354
-Yeah, she was out hiking with her friend.
-Wait. Mickey was hiking?

168
00:08:00,437 --> 00:08:01,814
-[Wade] Yeah.
-With what friend?

169
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:03,315
-Shaun or...
-No, it was some guy.

170
00:08:03,399 --> 00:08:04,734
-Was a dude.
-Some guy?

171
00:08:04,817 --> 00:08:06,903
-[Chris] All right. Let me at him!
-Hey!

172
00:08:06,986 --> 00:08:08,154
-Welcome back, man.
-[Wade] Love you, man.

173
00:08:08,237 --> 00:08:09,531
[Gus] Hey, guys. Thanks for coming over.

174
00:08:09,614 --> 00:08:11,866
-It was good to see you.
-Great to see you. I'm glad you're back.

175
00:08:11,949 --> 00:08:13,200
-I appreciate it.
-See you.

176
00:08:13,284 --> 00:08:14,869
-Let me know about that Nintendo 64.
-Sure.

177
00:08:14,952 --> 00:08:17,288
-Yeah, yeah. Okay. Bye.
-[Beth] Bye!

178
00:08:17,371 --> 00:08:18,706
[chuckles]

179
00:08:26,464 --> 00:08:27,673
[cell phone chimes]

180
00:08:39,435 --> 00:08:40,895
[Mickey] Hey!

181
00:08:40,978 --> 00:08:41,979
Hey.

182
00:08:42,730 --> 00:08:44,023
You look tan.

183
00:08:44,816 --> 00:08:47,109
-Really? Do I?
-Uh... I don't know.

184
00:08:47,193 --> 00:08:50,071
Feel like that's what people say
when someone comes back from a trip.

185
00:08:50,154 --> 00:08:52,489
Well, then,
let's just say I look super tan.

186
00:08:57,328 --> 00:08:58,454
Hey.

187
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,628
-You want to order something?
-Sure. Yeah.

188
00:09:06,588 --> 00:09:08,380
So, how have you been?

189
00:09:08,464 --> 00:09:10,341
Good. Good to be back. Yeah.

190
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:13,970
-How about you? How are you?
-Good. Good. Yeah.

191
00:09:22,353 --> 00:09:23,520
[scatting]

192
00:09:23,605 --> 00:09:26,899
Things got, uh... pretty crazy
between the two of us there.

193
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:28,735
Yeah, I know.

194
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:31,571
Time apart can really, uh,
fuck up a relationship.

195
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:34,323
I mean, that's what happened
to my best friends, Katy and Russell.

196
00:09:34,406 --> 00:09:35,617
Who?

197
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:37,243
Oh, did I not tell you?

198
00:09:37,326 --> 00:09:40,412
My best friends are Katy Perry
and Russell Brand?

199
00:09:40,496 --> 00:09:43,791
-No, you never mentioned that.
-Yeah, yeah. They're good kids.

200
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:45,417
-[man] How's it going?
-Hey.

201
00:09:45,501 --> 00:09:48,129
Can I get, um, a soy latte?

202
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:51,758
And I will take a ordinary latte.

203
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:53,676
-Ha! I got it.
-Thank you.

204
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:55,595
Ah. Thanks, Mickey.

205
00:09:56,137 --> 00:09:59,766
And, hey, I just want to say,
you know, as far as us being apart, I...

206
00:10:00,892 --> 00:10:03,811
I know I could have handled things better.
I was way out of line there.

207
00:10:03,895 --> 00:10:06,438
-It's fine, whatever.
-No, Mickey.

208
00:10:06,522 --> 00:10:07,732
I'm serious.

209
00:10:07,815 --> 00:10:10,902
You're right. I am very codependent.

210
00:10:10,985 --> 00:10:12,862
And it's scary for me
to look at my own shit,

211
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:15,281
so I focus on yours 'cause it's easier,

212
00:10:15,364 --> 00:10:18,325
and that's just super unfair to you,
and...

213
00:10:18,409 --> 00:10:19,493
I am sorry.

214
00:10:21,245 --> 00:10:23,497
I... I appreciate that. Thank you.

215
00:10:23,580 --> 00:10:25,291
Yeah. I just... I don't know, I gotta...

216
00:10:25,374 --> 00:10:28,002
try my best,
just look at my own shit, you know?

217
00:10:28,085 --> 00:10:29,962
-Well, Al-Anon can help with that.
-Hmm.

218
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:32,882
Yeah. Well, I've actually gone
to a few meetings, so...

219
00:10:32,965 --> 00:10:36,969
What? Really?
Gus, that's amazing. I'm so proud of you.

220
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:40,139
-Ah.
-Um, I'm sorry. That was condescending.

221
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:42,433
No. No, no. Not at all.

222
00:10:43,392 --> 00:10:44,518
-[man] There you go.
-Hey.

223
00:10:44,601 --> 00:10:46,478
[Mickey] Really? You've never?

224
00:10:46,562 --> 00:10:48,397
I'm serious. I've never had a wet dream.

225
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:50,149
-Oh, my God.
-It's weird. I know.

226
00:10:50,232 --> 00:10:51,818
-[cell phone vibrating]
-I don't know why. [chuckles]

227
00:10:55,404 --> 00:10:56,405
Oh.

228
00:10:57,323 --> 00:10:59,116
You can reply to that if you need to.
It's cool.

229
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,827
-It's fine. Yeah.
-You sure? Okay.

230
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:03,245
Do you have any, uh, plans today?

231
00:11:03,329 --> 00:11:04,914
What are your Saturday plans?

232
00:11:04,997 --> 00:11:08,250
I'm doing the laundry.
I am paying my bills.

233
00:11:08,918 --> 00:11:10,962
I'm going to the post office.

234
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:14,631
Just some... real exciting shit, Mickey.

235
00:11:14,716 --> 00:11:18,594
Hmm. Well, maybe you could come by
my place later? Like, 9:00 or 10:00?

236
00:11:18,677 --> 00:11:20,722
Yeah. Sure.

237
00:11:33,109 --> 00:11:35,694
I'm glad you're back. I missed you.

238
00:11:37,071 --> 00:11:38,155
I missed you, too.

239
00:11:40,908 --> 00:11:44,120
Hey, remember that time I went to Atlanta
and we both flipped out?

240
00:11:44,203 --> 00:11:47,456
-Oh... such fond memories.
-[chuckles]

241
00:12:05,808 --> 00:12:07,977
-[Dustin] You gotta taste this sauce.
-[Mickey] What?

242
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:09,937
Taste this sauce I made. It is amazing.

243
00:12:11,272 --> 00:12:13,440
Mmm. That was really hot.

244
00:12:13,524 --> 00:12:15,234
Oh, sorry, should've warned you.

245
00:12:15,317 --> 00:12:18,529
But it's good, right?
I am killing it with sauces lately.

246
00:12:18,946 --> 00:12:20,322
Yeah, it's good.

247
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:21,532
Yeah, but you taste better.

248
00:12:22,574 --> 00:12:23,742
Mmm, thank you.

249
00:12:25,327 --> 00:12:27,079
What's wrong? You're acting weird.

250
00:12:30,082 --> 00:12:32,543
I don't think we should do this anymore.

251
00:12:38,215 --> 00:12:39,216
Do what?

252
00:12:40,176 --> 00:12:42,804
You and me. All of it.

253
00:12:42,887 --> 00:12:44,638
It's moving...

254
00:12:45,807 --> 00:12:47,099
too fast.

255
00:12:47,183 --> 00:12:49,560
It's getting too serious,
and I'm not ready for it.

256
00:12:49,643 --> 00:12:52,146
I think we should break it off.

257
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:01,197
[clicks tongue]

258
00:13:02,156 --> 00:13:03,532
I guess we should.

259
00:13:06,743 --> 00:13:08,537
Okay, uh, I'm gonna go.

260
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:10,539
I guess you are.

261
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:13,792
-All right, take care.
-I will take care.

262
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:18,339
Are you okay? 'Cause you, like, seem okay,
but, like, scary okay.

263
00:13:18,422 --> 00:13:20,424
-You should go now.
-[pot clangs]

264
00:13:20,507 --> 00:13:22,593
[softly] Okay. All right.

265
00:13:22,676 --> 00:13:24,595
Is this because that guy is back in town?

266
00:13:24,678 --> 00:13:27,389
The little tree sprite?
The one at the Springwood? Gus?

267
00:13:27,473 --> 00:13:29,892
No! This has nothing to do with him.

268
00:13:29,976 --> 00:13:33,104
Yeah, that guy will...
never make you happy.

269
00:13:34,313 --> 00:13:36,148
But I guess you want to be unhappy.

270
00:13:36,232 --> 00:13:38,775
Okay, yeah, you've got me all figured out.

271
00:13:39,735 --> 00:13:41,737
-Goodbye, Dustin.
-Goodbye, whore!

272
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:45,657
See? There it goes!
You called me a whore again.

273
00:13:45,741 --> 00:13:48,119
You are the same. This is all the same.

274
00:13:50,913 --> 00:13:52,999
[door opens and slams]

275
00:13:55,834 --> 00:13:57,044
[exhales]

276
00:13:59,796 --> 00:14:01,007
[sighs]

277
00:14:03,634 --> 00:14:06,470
[music playing faintly over speakers]

278
00:14:07,889 --> 00:14:12,059
Bertie, I'm sorry for putting you
in an awkward situation with Dustin.

279
00:14:12,143 --> 00:14:14,353
That really was not fair of me.

280
00:14:14,436 --> 00:14:17,814
Oh, okay. I'm not mad anymore.

281
00:14:17,899 --> 00:14:20,401
I spoke to my mom about it, and she said,

282
00:14:20,484 --> 00:14:23,487
"Bertie, you're judging Mickey."
And my mom's right.

283
00:14:23,570 --> 00:14:25,031
And who am I to judge?

284
00:14:25,114 --> 00:14:29,076
I'm hooking back up with Randy again.
I mean, what the fuck am I doing?

285
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:32,829
He only could pay me back 'cause
he borrowed more money from his family.

286
00:14:32,914 --> 00:14:35,124
He's really excited
about his new job at the moment,

287
00:14:35,207 --> 00:14:37,709
which is being in the background
of a TV show.

288
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:38,961
He's in his 30s.

289
00:14:39,045 --> 00:14:40,546
Also, he loves it

290
00:14:40,629 --> 00:14:44,300
because he gets to lie on a gurney
during his lunch hour.

291
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:45,968
-[chuckles]
-What am I doing?

292
00:14:46,052 --> 00:14:47,553
Why did I go back?

293
00:14:47,636 --> 00:14:50,097
They say that you go back
to painful situations

294
00:14:50,181 --> 00:14:52,266
because they're comfortable and familiar.

295
00:14:53,809 --> 00:14:54,810
I hear that.

296
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:57,646
Sometimes when I'm in pain, I'm like,
"Hello, old friend."

297
00:14:57,729 --> 00:15:02,234
Yeah. I'm very comfortable with pain.
It's the happy part I'm not used to.

298
00:15:02,318 --> 00:15:05,237
Right. We need to get comfortable
with the happy part.

299
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:06,863
-Yeah.
-Definitely.

300
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:10,117
-Do you want the rest of this yogurt?
-No...

301
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:12,870
All right, then.
It's goin' back in the fridge.

302
00:15:15,081 --> 00:15:18,834
Hey, Bertie, Gus is coming over tonight,
if you can handle that.

303
00:15:18,918 --> 00:15:21,963
Oh... sure.

304
00:15:22,046 --> 00:15:25,841
I mean... I definitely won't tell him
about Dustin,

305
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:30,179
but I should probably tell you,
I've been told I'm a terrible liar.

306
00:15:30,262 --> 00:15:33,432
I mean, I don't think so.
I think I'm quite convincing,

307
00:15:33,515 --> 00:15:36,060
but people have told me
I'm really very bad at it.

308
00:15:37,269 --> 00:15:39,188
Well, I ended things with Dustin today,

309
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:40,856
-if that makes it any easier.
-Really?

310
00:15:40,939 --> 00:15:42,066
How did that go down?

311
00:15:42,149 --> 00:15:46,862
You know how some guys when they're angry
are like, tick, tick... boom?

312
00:15:46,945 --> 00:15:48,322
Dustin's like tick, boom!

313
00:15:48,405 --> 00:15:50,491
You should've seen the look in his eye.
I mean...

314
00:15:50,574 --> 00:15:53,827
I didn't know
if I was gonna get out of there alive.

315
00:15:53,910 --> 00:15:56,538
Right. Are you gonna tell Gus
about any of this?

316
00:15:56,622 --> 00:15:59,375
No! Jesus, that would just hurt him.

317
00:15:59,458 --> 00:16:00,542
What if he asks?

318
00:16:00,626 --> 00:16:04,838
If he asks me if I've slept
with anybody else, then I will say yes.

319
00:16:04,921 --> 00:16:05,964
I'm not gonna lie.

320
00:16:06,048 --> 00:16:09,093
But I wasn't really
breaking the rules or whatever.

321
00:16:09,176 --> 00:16:11,428
Huh. Okay.

322
00:16:11,512 --> 00:16:12,972
[knock on door]

323
00:16:17,226 --> 00:16:18,810
-Hi! [chuckles]
-Hey, hey!

324
00:16:18,894 --> 00:16:20,312
-Hi, Mickey.
-Hi.

325
00:16:20,396 --> 00:16:22,231
-Hey!
-Hey, great to see you!

326
00:16:22,314 --> 00:16:23,857
It's good to see you, too. How are you?

327
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:26,068
Gus, the craziest thing happened
at work today.

328
00:16:26,152 --> 00:16:27,569
You won't even believe it.

329
00:16:27,653 --> 00:16:31,865
There was this man, and he ate so many
Steak-umms, and he threw up everywhere,

330
00:16:31,948 --> 00:16:35,452
but then he still was like, "I love 'em!"
[chuckles] It was so stupid.

331
00:16:35,536 --> 00:16:36,870
-Oh, that's, uh...
-It was crazy!

332
00:16:36,953 --> 00:16:39,123
-I can see how that's funny.
-I'm gonna text my mom about it.

333
00:16:39,206 --> 00:16:41,833
Okay. Good to see ya.

334
00:16:41,917 --> 00:16:44,878
Ooh, that's a nasty little stain there.

335
00:16:44,961 --> 00:16:47,339
-Oh, yeah, it's wine. [sighs]
-Oh.

336
00:16:49,466 --> 00:16:51,343
I wasn't drinking.

337
00:16:51,427 --> 00:16:53,054
Okay, I wasn't saying anything.

338
00:16:53,137 --> 00:16:55,556
No, it was Bertie.
She had a full glass of wine

339
00:16:55,639 --> 00:16:59,226
and stubbed her toe on the coffee table
and it just spilled.

340
00:16:59,310 --> 00:17:00,977
It's all good. I don't care.

341
00:17:01,853 --> 00:17:03,230
[Mickey moans softly]

342
00:17:08,235 --> 00:17:09,570
-[Gus grunts]
-[sighs]

343
00:17:09,653 --> 00:17:12,156
I'm sorry that I acted so shitty
when we were apart.

344
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:13,532
-I--
-It's okay. Don't--

345
00:17:13,615 --> 00:17:15,867
-No, I feel--
-I... I was...

346
00:17:15,951 --> 00:17:17,869
making you that way. It's fine.

347
00:17:17,953 --> 00:17:21,707
I think it's, like I said,
I'm really bad with separation, and...

348
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:23,959
it made me act out and I'm...

349
00:17:25,043 --> 00:17:27,171
I'm sorry. I think I'm...

350
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:30,507
way more into you than I even know.

351
00:17:31,717 --> 00:17:32,884
Aw.

352
00:17:33,886 --> 00:17:35,053
Well, me, too.

353
00:17:35,637 --> 00:17:39,725
I mean, I'm into you, not me.

354
00:17:39,808 --> 00:17:42,186
-Or... you get it.
-Hey, hey, I have a question for you.

355
00:17:42,269 --> 00:17:43,187
What? What?

356
00:17:43,812 --> 00:17:49,818
What do you always wanna do in bed,
but you're too nervous to ask for?

357
00:17:50,986 --> 00:17:53,614
Oh, uh... I don't know.

358
00:17:53,697 --> 00:17:58,077
Okay, well,
what have you always wanted to do,

359
00:17:58,160 --> 00:18:00,496
but you've never done?
'Cause I wanna do that.

360
00:18:01,455 --> 00:18:03,207
Oh, my God. That's so much pressure.

361
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:06,293
That's like one of those things
I wish I had an answer for.

362
00:18:07,253 --> 00:18:08,670
You in your mind imagine,

363
00:18:08,754 --> 00:18:10,547
"Oh, I hope somebody asks me
this question."

364
00:18:10,631 --> 00:18:12,841
But I... I don't know.
I don't like talking...

365
00:18:12,924 --> 00:18:14,801
[inhales deeply] about sex.

366
00:18:14,885 --> 00:18:17,471
I'm up for anything in the moment, Mickey.

367
00:18:17,554 --> 00:18:20,724
What if I, like, put a finger up your ass?

368
00:18:20,807 --> 00:18:22,434
-Uh, maybe.
-Yeah?

369
00:18:22,518 --> 00:18:24,645
Yeah, just don't give me
a heads-up beforehand.

370
00:18:24,728 --> 00:18:27,022
It's like, I don't wanna know
the end of a movie before it happens.

371
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:29,941
May I feel free to make a bold choice?

372
00:18:30,025 --> 00:18:31,610
-Yes. [chuckles]
-Okay.

373
00:18:31,693 --> 00:18:32,986
Make a bold choice.

374
00:18:42,746 --> 00:18:44,039
[yawns]

375
00:18:56,051 --> 00:18:57,886
-Good morning.
-[inhales deeply]

376
00:18:57,969 --> 00:19:00,181
[grunts softly] Good morning.

377
00:19:02,849 --> 00:19:04,100
[cell phone vibrating]

378
00:19:11,483 --> 00:19:13,819
[Mickey] Sounds like my phone's
blowing up. Can you hand it to me?

379
00:19:14,403 --> 00:19:15,737
[inhales deeply]

380
00:19:15,821 --> 00:19:17,781
-[grunts] Okay.
-[cell phone continues vibrating]

381
00:19:28,209 --> 00:19:29,626
Hey. [clears throat]

382
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:31,337
Gus-Gus, let's get out of here.

383
00:19:33,339 --> 00:19:35,216
Really? We just woke up.

384
00:19:35,299 --> 00:19:36,675
I know, but I'm feelin' antsy.

385
00:19:36,758 --> 00:19:39,010
Let's get out of here.
Let's do something fun.

386
00:19:39,595 --> 00:19:40,429
Mmm.

387
00:19:42,848 --> 00:19:44,308
-Look at you.
-What are you doing?

388
00:19:44,391 --> 00:19:46,059
-I want to take your picture.
-No.

389
00:19:46,142 --> 00:19:48,645
-What?
-Morning photos are really nasty.

390
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:49,813
-Are you serious?
-Yeah.

391
00:19:49,896 --> 00:19:51,106
Morning photos are the best.

392
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:55,360
You got messed up hair, little puffy eyes.
People are at their cutest in the morning.

393
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:56,695
-I'm serious.
-I love it. What?

394
00:19:56,778 --> 00:19:58,905
Let's go do something.
What do you wanna do?

395
00:19:58,989 --> 00:20:00,782
You know what I always thought
could be fun?

396
00:20:00,866 --> 00:20:04,160
Uh, at the park they have, uh...
They have paddleboating.

397
00:20:04,245 --> 00:20:05,912
Perfect. Yeah, let's do it.

398
00:20:05,996 --> 00:20:07,373
-You wanna paddleboat?
-Mmm-hmm.

399
00:20:07,456 --> 00:20:08,415
Okay.

400
00:20:09,082 --> 00:20:10,501
Um...

401
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:11,918
-I gotta piss first.
-Okay.

402
00:20:12,002 --> 00:20:13,462
-Okay.
-Quick piss.

403
00:20:14,921 --> 00:20:17,216
-[groaning]
-Come on, Gus. I'm serious.

404
00:20:17,299 --> 00:20:19,134
Okay, okay.

405
00:20:19,217 --> 00:20:20,636
Oh, fuck.

406
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:23,305
I thought you weren't
a morning person either.

407
00:20:23,389 --> 00:20:24,598
That's why I like you.

408
00:20:24,681 --> 00:20:27,058
-[sighs]
-But you're... Okay, okay.

409
00:20:27,142 --> 00:20:28,560
[cell phone vibrating]

410
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:38,194
[softly] Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

411
00:20:41,407 --> 00:20:43,492
[Gus] All right. Initiating paddleboat.

412
00:20:43,575 --> 00:20:45,452
Five, four...

413
00:20:45,536 --> 00:20:47,704
three, two...

414
00:20:48,914 --> 00:20:50,374
Fun?

415
00:20:55,754 --> 00:20:56,880
[knocking on door]

416
00:21:01,302 --> 00:21:02,761
-Hey.
-Oh, hey, Dustin. How are you?

417
00:21:02,844 --> 00:21:04,638
-I'm well. How are you?
-I'm good.

418
00:21:04,721 --> 00:21:06,848
-Oh, do... Come in!
-Thanks.

419
00:21:07,599 --> 00:21:10,727
-Uh, is Mickey here?
-Uh, no.

420
00:21:11,437 --> 00:21:13,355
No. She... she stepped out.

421
00:21:13,439 --> 00:21:16,400
Okay. Do you know where she went?
Is she coming back soon?

422
00:21:16,483 --> 00:21:17,734
No.

423
00:21:17,818 --> 00:21:20,153
I don't know. She didn't say.

424
00:21:20,236 --> 00:21:21,280
Don't know.

425
00:21:21,363 --> 00:21:23,824
Okay. Just, uh, tell her I dropped by?

426
00:21:23,907 --> 00:21:25,451
Or, you know, don't worry about it.

427
00:21:25,534 --> 00:21:27,536
You know what? Let her know.

428
00:21:28,287 --> 00:21:30,831
-Okay. I'll give her the message.
-Okay.

429
00:21:31,582 --> 00:21:34,876
-Uh, also, I think I left a jacket here?
-Oh, I haven't seen one.

430
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:36,086
What does it look like?

431
00:21:36,169 --> 00:21:38,755
Uh, it's like a letterman's jacket
type thing.

432
00:21:38,839 --> 00:21:41,216
-Cool.
-I may have left it in Mickey's room.

433
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:42,884
Would you mind checking?

434
00:21:42,968 --> 00:21:44,345
I would go in there,
I just don't wanna root around

435
00:21:44,428 --> 00:21:45,429
in her stuff when she's not here.

436
00:21:45,512 --> 00:21:47,097
Oh, okay, sure. I'll go have a look.

437
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:48,349
Thank you.

438
00:22:06,116 --> 00:22:07,451
[Bertie] What color is it?

439
00:22:08,118 --> 00:22:09,995
Uh, it's black and gold.

440
00:22:10,078 --> 00:22:11,497
[Bertie] That sounds nice.

441
00:22:18,587 --> 00:22:20,422
Sorry, Dustin, I've looked everywhere.

442
00:22:20,506 --> 00:22:23,008
-There's no sign of it. Sorry.
-No sign of it?

443
00:22:23,091 --> 00:22:24,843
Okay, no worries.
I'll keep looking for it.

444
00:22:24,926 --> 00:22:27,638
It'll turn up somewhere.
I will, uh, see you around.

445
00:22:27,721 --> 00:22:28,805
-[Bertie] Okay.
-Thanks again.

446
00:22:29,473 --> 00:22:30,599
Weird.

447
00:22:35,729 --> 00:22:38,399
So, yeah, I guess, like, a few years ago,
they drained this lake,

448
00:22:38,482 --> 00:22:41,526
and everybody was expecting
to find all these dead bodies.

449
00:22:41,943 --> 00:22:44,237
But then when they did it,
there were no dead bodies,

450
00:22:44,320 --> 00:22:46,072
and everybody was weirdly disappointed.
[chuckles]

451
00:22:48,825 --> 00:22:50,201
Glad you're back.

452
00:22:50,285 --> 00:22:52,788
Aw. I'm glad I'm back, too.

453
00:22:57,834 --> 00:22:59,420
[inhales deeply] It feels good.

454
00:23:16,728 --> 00:23:17,896
[Gus] You know what's cool?

455
00:23:17,979 --> 00:23:22,108
We both have the names
of Disney mice, right?

456
00:23:22,192 --> 00:23:24,778
'Cause I'm Gus-Gus from Cinderella,

457
00:23:24,861 --> 00:23:28,406
you're Mickey, as in the classic mouse.

458
00:23:28,490 --> 00:23:29,950
-Mickey Mouse, yeah.
-Yeah.

459
00:23:30,033 --> 00:23:31,284
You like being reminded of that

460
00:23:31,367 --> 00:23:33,495
-I'm sure, right?
-Mmm-hmm.

461
00:23:33,579 --> 00:23:34,663
[Gus] Oh, cool.

462
00:23:38,750 --> 00:23:40,627
Uh, you know what?
Can we get some broccoli?

463
00:23:40,711 --> 00:23:42,378
'Cause I really, um...

464
00:23:42,463 --> 00:23:45,173
I'm just feeling
like I need more broccoli.

465
00:23:45,256 --> 00:23:47,342
And I also really have to go
to the bathroom,

466
00:23:47,425 --> 00:23:50,011
so maybe you can get the broccoli,

467
00:23:50,095 --> 00:23:51,763
-and I'll meet you--
-Are you okay?

468
00:23:51,847 --> 00:23:53,474
-[Mickey] Yeah.
-[Gus] You seem jumpy.

469
00:23:53,557 --> 00:23:55,642
[Mickey] Ugh, when I gotta pee I'm...
Um...

470
00:23:55,725 --> 00:23:58,603
Ask a lot of questions, make sure
you don't get, uh, ripped off, okay?

471
00:24:17,873 --> 00:24:21,627
[man] Fresh strawberries!
Papayas! Oranges!

472
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:24,880
Lemon! Grapefruit! We got melons!

473
00:24:25,881 --> 00:24:27,465
-Pineapple?
-Sorry, hi.

474
00:24:27,549 --> 00:24:28,592
[man] Oh.

475
00:24:29,217 --> 00:24:30,426
[whispers] Gus! Gus, hi.

476
00:24:30,511 --> 00:24:32,095
Hey, how's it going?

477
00:24:32,178 --> 00:24:33,429
Hey, I got your broccoli.

478
00:24:33,514 --> 00:24:35,932
I haggled him down to $1,000.
I think that's fair, right?

479
00:24:36,016 --> 00:24:37,643
Yeah, you want to get out of here?

480
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:39,686
I'm having a good time.
You want to check out a few more booths

481
00:24:39,770 --> 00:24:41,688
-and then maybe head home?
-Uh...

482
00:24:42,772 --> 00:24:45,859
Yeah, um,
how about I get you a massage?

483
00:24:45,942 --> 00:24:47,528
-I don't know. I don't need it.
-Come on!

484
00:24:47,611 --> 00:24:49,404
You got me broccoli.
I'll get you a massage.

485
00:24:49,487 --> 00:24:50,989
-Okay.
-Yeah, I'm getting that for you.

486
00:24:51,072 --> 00:24:52,533
-What? Wow. Thanks.
-Mmm-hmm. Yeah.

487
00:24:52,616 --> 00:24:54,660
[Gus] That actually would be amazing
right now.

488
00:25:00,290 --> 00:25:01,208
Hey!

489
00:25:22,979 --> 00:25:25,732
-Hey, would you like some strawberries?
-Uh, no. No, thank you.

490
00:25:43,584 --> 00:25:46,127
[girls screaming and laughing]

491
00:25:46,211 --> 00:25:47,629
[man] You're a little tense in here.

492
00:25:47,713 --> 00:25:49,673
[Gus] Yeah,
I get really tense in my neck.

493
00:25:49,756 --> 00:25:50,799
-[man] Wow.
-[Gus] Yeah.

494
00:25:50,882 --> 00:25:52,634
-[man] Do you work out a lot?
-[chuckles]

495
00:25:52,718 --> 00:25:54,010
-[Gus] No. [chuckles]
-Really?

496
00:25:54,094 --> 00:25:55,971
-Construction work?
-[Gus] You flatter me.

497
00:25:56,054 --> 00:25:57,388
[man] Pressure point for all--

498
00:25:57,472 --> 00:25:59,265
Hey. Okay, uh, you ready to go?

499
00:25:59,349 --> 00:26:00,726
-Here you go.
-Huh?

500
00:26:00,809 --> 00:26:01,810
We just started.

501
00:26:01,893 --> 00:26:05,063
-It's hot. Feels like I'm gonna pass out.
-Yeah, sorry. Okay.

502
00:26:05,146 --> 00:26:07,190
-Thanks, so much.
-Mickey, this is Kent, by the way.

503
00:26:12,195 --> 00:26:13,279
[man] What the...

504
00:26:14,698 --> 00:26:15,699
No!

505
00:26:27,502 --> 00:26:29,379
-[Gus exhales] Ooh.
-[sighs] Oh, my God.

506
00:26:29,462 --> 00:26:31,464
It feels so good to be back inside.

507
00:26:32,132 --> 00:26:34,092
Sorry I was acting so weird back there.

508
00:26:34,175 --> 00:26:37,137
When I'm out in the sun for too long,
it kinda fries my brain.

509
00:26:37,220 --> 00:26:39,765
Oh, totally understand. It's all good.

510
00:26:39,848 --> 00:26:41,182
You don't have to convince me

511
00:26:41,266 --> 00:26:44,019
that the indoors are always better
than the outdoors.

512
00:26:44,102 --> 00:26:47,773
You know... I'm gonna get a soda
from the vending machine.

513
00:26:47,856 --> 00:26:50,483
-You want anything?
-Yeah, anything. Surprise me.

514
00:26:50,567 --> 00:26:53,611
All right, I will BRB.

515
00:26:54,905 --> 00:26:57,115
That's how the cool kids say
"be right back."

516
00:27:07,208 --> 00:27:08,418
[sighs]

517
00:27:13,882 --> 00:27:15,801
[Dustin] Excuse me,
do you know Gus Cruikshank?

518
00:27:17,803 --> 00:27:20,221
Hey, uh, [clears throat]
do you know my buddy Gus Cruikshank?

519
00:27:20,305 --> 00:27:21,556
-Who?
-Yeah.

520
00:27:21,639 --> 00:27:23,558
Do you guys know Gus Cruikshank
by any chance?

521
00:27:23,641 --> 00:27:26,770
All I'm saying is, you could've given us
a bigger heads up on this gray paint.

522
00:27:26,853 --> 00:27:29,480
That's, like, your one job
on the committee council.

523
00:27:29,564 --> 00:27:33,276
We put fliers announcing the change
in everyone's mailbox.

524
00:27:33,359 --> 00:27:36,863
Well, I'm sorry, but I didn't get one,
and I'm not okay with the change.

525
00:27:36,947 --> 00:27:41,034
-Gray is sad.
-Gray is sophisticated, elegant and cool.

526
00:27:41,117 --> 00:27:42,869
Excuse me,
either of you know Gus Cruikshank?

527
00:27:42,953 --> 00:27:44,120
-Yeah, he's my buddy.
-Great.

528
00:27:44,204 --> 00:27:46,039
We were just at the farmers market
with Mickey.

529
00:27:46,122 --> 00:27:47,623
I know Mickey, too. Great girl!

530
00:27:47,708 --> 00:27:48,959
-Yeah. My phone died.
-[Chris] Huh.

531
00:27:49,042 --> 00:27:50,711
And I don't know where Gus' place is.

532
00:27:50,794 --> 00:27:52,295
I'm pretty sure they came back here.

533
00:27:52,378 --> 00:27:55,799
Oh, yeah, this happens all the time.
Gus is over in Building E. Second floor.

534
00:27:55,882 --> 00:27:57,926
I want to say E-232.

535
00:27:58,009 --> 00:27:59,928
Two-thirty-two. Great.
Thanks. Appreciate it.

536
00:28:00,011 --> 00:28:01,512
No problem. Happy to help, amigo!

537
00:28:01,596 --> 00:28:03,264
[knocking on door]

538
00:28:04,682 --> 00:28:06,059
All right, cool your jets.

539
00:28:06,142 --> 00:28:07,477
[knocking continues]

540
00:28:09,771 --> 00:28:10,772
Is he here?

541
00:28:11,689 --> 00:28:13,566
-Fuck, dude!
-We need to talk.

542
00:28:13,649 --> 00:28:15,485
No, we do not need to talk.

543
00:28:15,568 --> 00:28:17,528
I'm not leaving until we talk!

544
00:28:19,030 --> 00:28:20,866
Okay, all right.

545
00:28:21,825 --> 00:28:22,826
Okay.

546
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:24,577
[lock clicks]

547
00:28:24,660 --> 00:28:27,205
Dude, what the fuck is going on with you?

548
00:28:27,288 --> 00:28:30,416
You're chasing me around a farmers market?
You're stalking me?

549
00:28:30,500 --> 00:28:32,252
I am doing what I didn't do last time.

550
00:28:32,335 --> 00:28:34,045
I'm fighting for you.

551
00:28:34,129 --> 00:28:35,881
Well, don't. I don't want you to.

552
00:28:35,964 --> 00:28:37,883
Can you just please go
before Gus gets back?

553
00:28:37,966 --> 00:28:40,969
I wanna be here when he gets back.
I want to tell him about us.

554
00:28:41,052 --> 00:28:43,471
So you... you want to ruin this for me?

555
00:28:43,555 --> 00:28:47,517
Yes. I want to tell him about us.
And then, he's gonna leave you,

556
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:51,229
[stutters] and you and I can get back
to making this work, okay?

557
00:28:51,312 --> 00:28:54,399
[stutters] This is the story
we're gonna tell our kids.

558
00:28:54,482 --> 00:28:57,485
"Your mom was dating a loser,
and I... I came after her.

559
00:28:57,568 --> 00:28:59,112
I chased after her." All right?

560
00:28:59,195 --> 00:29:02,032
This... this guy is a wimp.
He's not gonna fight for you.

561
00:29:02,115 --> 00:29:04,117
You want someone
who is gonna fight for you!

562
00:29:04,200 --> 00:29:07,328
No, Dustin, I don't. Please, I don't.

563
00:29:07,412 --> 00:29:10,749
You don't know
what the fuck you want, okay?

564
00:29:11,166 --> 00:29:12,417
I'm being direct with you.

565
00:29:12,500 --> 00:29:16,922
This fucking guy is not the answer
to your problems, okay?

566
00:29:17,005 --> 00:29:19,424
You need to have the courage
to stay in the game with me

567
00:29:19,507 --> 00:29:21,301
until we figure this out together.

568
00:29:21,384 --> 00:29:24,595
Dustin... just let me go.

569
00:29:24,679 --> 00:29:26,973
Maybe with Gus I can be happy.

570
00:29:29,684 --> 00:29:32,270
[chuckles] You're gonna destroy him.

571
00:29:32,353 --> 00:29:34,147
Maybe I will. Maybe.

572
00:29:34,230 --> 00:29:36,732
But let me figure that out
on my own, okay?

573
00:29:36,817 --> 00:29:40,195
If you love me,
you're gonna give me the space to do that.

574
00:29:45,283 --> 00:29:46,659
[doorknob rattling]

575
00:29:46,742 --> 00:29:48,453
[Gus] Hello? Mickey?

576
00:29:49,662 --> 00:29:50,997
[knocking on door]

577
00:29:51,081 --> 00:29:52,748
-[Gus] Mickey?
-[whispering] Can you--

578
00:29:52,833 --> 00:29:54,417
Can you just go out there, please?

579
00:29:58,588 --> 00:30:00,006
[knocking on door]

580
00:30:00,966 --> 00:30:02,258
[Gus] Mickey?

581
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:06,847
-Hello?
-[knocks on door]

582
00:30:11,142 --> 00:30:13,394
-You there?
-[Mickey] I'm coming, Gus! Sorry!

583
00:30:15,021 --> 00:30:16,022
Sorry.

584
00:30:16,982 --> 00:30:18,316
-Um...
-Hey, what's up?

585
00:30:18,399 --> 00:30:20,735
Hi, I was in the bathroom
and I locked the door

586
00:30:20,819 --> 00:30:22,946
'cause I didn't want anyone
to be able to get in.

587
00:30:23,029 --> 00:30:26,157
Oh, it's okay. I don't trust anybody
around here. It's fine.

588
00:30:26,241 --> 00:30:27,993
Uh, hope you like Sprite.

589
00:30:28,076 --> 00:30:31,872
Oh, well, I'm...
I'm more of a 7 Up girl, actually.

590
00:30:31,955 --> 00:30:34,082
It's okay. They literally taste the same.

591
00:30:36,376 --> 00:30:37,710
Hey, you okay?

592
00:30:38,711 --> 00:30:40,338
I... I gotta tell you something.

593
00:30:41,339 --> 00:30:43,758
Okay. Let's talk.

594
00:30:43,841 --> 00:30:47,387
Uh, yeah, it's um...
It's... it's kinda scary to say.

595
00:30:48,972 --> 00:30:50,015
Look...

596
00:30:51,016 --> 00:30:53,101
I know I've been coming on strong.
It's just...

597
00:30:53,184 --> 00:30:55,811
I think when I got back,
I just got excited--

598
00:30:55,896 --> 00:30:58,189
No, it's not that.
Gus, it's not. It's...

599
00:30:59,107 --> 00:31:00,108
[sighs]

600
00:31:02,443 --> 00:31:04,654
[stutters] I wanna be
in a relationship with you.

601
00:31:04,737 --> 00:31:06,739
[Beck's "True Love Will Find You
In The End" playing]

602
00:31:06,865 --> 00:31:09,700
-Okay. All right.
-Yeah.

603
00:31:09,784 --> 00:31:13,704
I don't wanna do
any more nonexclusive bullshit.

604
00:31:13,788 --> 00:31:15,290
That ends today.

605
00:31:15,373 --> 00:31:20,045
I wanna really try and work on this
and be in a real adult relationship.

606
00:31:23,173 --> 00:31:24,382
I want that, too.

607
00:31:25,341 --> 00:31:27,135
-Really?
-Of course.

608
00:31:29,054 --> 00:31:34,017
I'm in. Mickey, I'm in.
Let's... let's fucking be a couple.

609
00:31:34,100 --> 00:31:37,812
-Okay, let's... let's be a couple.
-We're a couple.

610
00:31:38,313 --> 00:31:43,359
♪ True love will find you in the end ♪

611
00:31:45,695 --> 00:31:47,655
♪ You'll find out just who... ♪

612
00:31:47,738 --> 00:31:48,739
[Mickey chuckles]

613
00:31:50,033 --> 00:31:51,618
-[Gus] I got you.
-Mmm-hmm.

614
00:31:51,701 --> 00:31:53,244
[balcony door opens]

615
00:31:53,328 --> 00:31:57,206
-♪ Don't be sad, I know you will ♪
-[balcony door closes]

616
00:32:00,376 --> 00:32:03,004
♪ Don't give up until ♪

617
00:32:03,630 --> 00:32:07,884
-♪ True love will find you in the end ♪
-[door opens and closes]

618
00:32:10,678 --> 00:32:15,224
♪ This is a promise with a catch ♪

619
00:32:18,186 --> 00:32:22,690
♪ Only if you're looking
Will it find you ♪

620
00:32:25,193 --> 00:32:30,698
♪ 'Cause true love is searching too ♪

621
00:32:32,617 --> 00:32:39,415
♪ How can it recognize you
Unless you step out into the light? ♪

622
00:32:42,627 --> 00:32:46,464
♪ Don't be sad, I know you will ♪

623
00:32:49,717 --> 00:32:52,136
♪ Don't give up until ♪

624
00:32:53,012 --> 00:32:58,393
♪ True love finds you in the end  ♪

625
00:32:59,894 --> 00:33:01,229
[harmonica playing]

626
00:33:18,830 --> 00:33:23,418
♪ True love will find you in the end ♪

